# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[use up]], to [[exhaust]]
#: {{syn|ca|exhaurir}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Han '''acabat''' els diners.|They have run out of money.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive|reflexive}} to [[use up]], to [[exhaust]]
#: {{syn|ca|exhaurir}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Ella s'ha '''acabat''' l'aigua.|She has run out of water.}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive|reflexive}} to [[run out]], to be [[use up|used up]]
#: {{uxi|ca|S'ha '''acabat''' l'aigua.|The water has run out.}}
#: {{ux|ca|s'ha '''acabat''' el bròquil!|that's enough!|footer=used to end a conversation, a list of objections, etc.|lit=The broccoli has run out}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to end
#: {{uxi|ca|Creia que el món '''acabaria'''|I/he/she thought the world was going to end}}
#: {{uxi|ca|On '''acaba''' aquest camí?|Where does this path end?}}
#: {{ux|ca|'''acabar''' com el rosari de l'aurora|to end up in fights and in an unfriendly way|lit=to end like the rosary at dawn}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive|reflexive}} to end
#: {{uxi|ca|Això no s''''acaba''' mai|This isn't ending ever}}
#: {{uxi|ca|El camí s''''acaba''' aquí|The path ends here.}}
# to have just done or completed something {{+preo|ca|de|infinitive}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Acaba''' d'arribar.|It has just arrived.}}
# {{lb|ca|in the negative}} to [[fail]] to do something {{+preo|ca|de|infinitive}}
#: {{uxi|ca|No ho '''acabo''' d'entendre.|I didn't understand that.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[end up]], [[wind up]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Acabarà''' penjat.|He'll end up hanged.}} 
# {{lb|ca|auxiliary followed by a gerund}} to get finally to do something or to reach a certain state
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Acabarà''' tornant|It will come again.}}
# to get finally to do something or to reach a certain state {{+preo|ca|per|infinitive}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Acabarà''' per no tornar.|It won't come again.}}

