===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|ab}} (Compare {{cog|pro|ab}}), from {{der|ca|la|apud}}. The addition of an ''-m-'' is very old, but it was not reflected in spelling until Fabra's orthography in the twentieth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Oriental}}
** {{a|before a vowel}} {{IPA|ca|/əmb/}}
** {{a|before a consonant}} {{IPA|ca|/əm/}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-amb.wav|Audio}}
*** {{homophones|ca|em}}
* ''{{a|Occidental}}''
** ''{{a|before a vowel}}'' {{IPA|ca|/amb/|/an/|/en/}}
** ''{{a|before a consonant}}'' {{IPA|ca|/am/|/an/|/en/}}
*** {{homophones|ca|en}}
** Notes: the standard pronunciations are /amb/ and /am/. The pronunciation /en/ is typically used in the Valencian Country and parts of Catalonia, the pronunciation /an/ is used in some southern parts of the Valencian Country.

