Page 3028 bacallà: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ca|nl|bakaliaw}}, of {{unc|ca|nocap=1}} origin.  Possibly from {{der|ca|la|baculum||stick, staff}}, referring to the way cod were split and dried on wooden sticks.

If the element *''bak-'' is a [[metathesis]] of *''kab-'' (compare {{cog|fr|cabillaud}} and {{cog|de|Kabeljau}} from {{cog|nl|kabeljauw}}), then the original form of the word could have been *''cabalao'', maybe meaning "large-headed fish". {{etydate|1640}}<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref>

Cognate to {{cog|it|baccalà}}, {{cog|pt|bacalhau}}, {{cog|es|bacalao}}.

===Pronunciation===
