Page 3606 benvinguda: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Literally, "well come". From {{compound|ca|ben|vinguda|t1=well|t2=come}}. Presumably a calque of {{cal|ca|frk|-|notext=1}} term, from {{der|ca|gem-pro|*wiljakwumô|t=a welcome guest or arrival}}, from which many modern Germanic forms descend, as {{cog|en|welcome}}.

The are many cognates in other [[Romance language]]s, such as {{cog|fr|bienvenu}}, {{cog|es|bienvenido}} and {{cog|it|benvenuto}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|bénvingúda}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f}}

