Page 4239 Bretanya: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ca|la|Britannia||Britain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Proper noun===
{{ca-proper noun|f}}

# {{transclude sense|ca|Brittany|id=region}}
# {{lb|ca|historical}} [[Brittania]] {{gloss|Great Britain and Brittany}}

====Usage notes====
The relationship between {{m|en|Great Britain}} and {{m|en|Brittany||Little Britain}} is clearer in Catalan than in English, at the cost of lacking a one word synonym for Great Britain. To refer to Roman Britain in Catalan, a later reborrowing from the same Latin origin, {{m|ca|Britània}}, is used.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|Gran Bretanya|gloss=Great Britain}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|Britània|gloss=Roman Britain}}
* {{l|ca|britànic}}

