Page 4495 ca: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|la|canis|canis, canem|t=dog}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m|#ns}}

# [[dog]]
#: {{syn|ca|gos<g:m>}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This term is used in Catalonia or Valencia only in stock phrases, with {{m|ca|gos}} (feminine {{m|ca|gossa}}) being the term generally used for a dog.
* In the Balearics, ''ca'' has retained its use as the primary word for a dog. However, instead of a feminine of ''ca'', {{m|ca||*cana}}, being used for a female dog, in the Balearics, {{m|ca|cussa}}, the feminine of {{m|ca|cus||little dog}} is used.
* Note also that those breeds of dogs that originated in the Balearics use ''ca'' and not {{m|ca|gos}} to form name of the breed.

=====Hyponyms=====
* {{qualifier|Balearics}} {{l|ca|cus||little dog|g=m}}, {{qualifier|Balearics}} {{l|ca|cussa||female dog|g=f}}
* {{l|ca|gos||male dog|g=m}}, {{l|ca|gossa||female dog|g=f}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|ca|{{l|ca|acanissar||to sic a dog on}}
|{{l|ca|ca de bestiar||Majorca Shepherd Dog}}
|{{l|ca|ca de bou||Majorca Mastiff}}
|{{l|ca|ca eivissenc||Ibizan Hound}}
|{{l|ca|Ca Major||Canis Majory}}
|{{l|ca|ca mè mallorquí||Majorcan Pointer}}
|{{l|ca|ca rater mallorquí||Majorcan Ratter}}
|ca petaner}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f|#s}}

# the letter [[K]] (lowercase [[k]])

=====Usage notes=====
* The letter K is not used in native Catalan words and thus its presence in a word is a fairly reliable indicator of a recent import.

===Etymology 3===
Apocopated form of {{m|ca|casa}}. Compare {{cog|fr|chez}}, {{cog|es|ca}}, {{cog|it|ca'}}.

====Particle====
{{head|ca|particle}}

# the [[house]] (of)
#: {{uxi|ca|Anem a '''ca''' la Maria.|We are going to Maria'''’s house'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Aquell casalot és '''cal''' Ramon.|That mansion is Ramon'''’s house'''.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Parlem català a '''ca''' nostra.|We speak Catalan at our '''house'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When followed by one of the articles {{m|ca|el}}, {{m|ca|els}}, {{m|ca|en}}, and {{m|ca|es}}, the word {{m|ca|ca}} contracts with them into {{m|ca|cal}}, {{m|ca|cals}}, {{m|ca|can}}, and {{m|ca|cas}}, respectively.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|cal}}, {{l|ca|cals}}, {{l|ca|can}}, {{l|ca|cas}}

