===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|VL.|capus||head, chief}}, from {{inh|ca|la|caput||head, etc.}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*kaput}}, ultimately from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*kauput-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*káput}}. Compare {{cog|oc|cap}}. Compare also {{m+|fr|personne}} (which can mean either "person" or "nobody").

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|anatomy}} [[head]]
# [[boss]], [[chief]], [[leader]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''cap''' d'estat|'''head''' of state}}
# {{lb|ca|landforms}} [[cape]] {{gloss|piece of land}}
# {{lb|ca|heraldry}} [[chief]]
# [[end]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''cap''' de setmana|week'''end'''}}

