Page 7539 creure: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|crēdō|crēdere}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*krezdō}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*ḱred dʰeh₁-||to place one's heart, i.e. to trust, believe}}, compound phrase of oblique case form of {{m|ine-pro|*ḱḗr||heart}} and {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-||to put, place, set}}. Compare {{cog|oc|creire}} or {{m|oc|créser}}, {{cog|fr|croire}}, {{cog|es|creer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ê}}<!-- from cawikt, confirmed by GDLC and DNV -->
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-creure.wav|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|root=ê}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive|reflexive}} to take as [[true]]
#: {{uxi|ca|No '''creguis''' res si no ho veus.|Don't believe anything if you don't see it.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|No '''et creguis''' res si no ho veus.|Don't believe anything if you don't see it.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[think]], to [[believe]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Creiem''' que no ella vindrà.|We think she won't come.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[believe]] as saying the [[truth]]
#: {{uxi|ca|Per què no em '''creus'''?|Why don't you believe me?}}
#* {{quote-web|ca|date=2020-12-07|author=Noelia Ramírez|url=https://cat.elpais.com/cat/2020/12/07/cultura/1607358920_635060.html|title=‘Gambito de dama’, tenim un problema (o per què les lletges de la literatura són maques a la pantalla)|work=El País|passage=Bàsicament, '''creu''' que la protagonista és massa atractiva per '''creure'''-se-la.|translation=Basically, he thinks that the female protagonist is too attractive to be believable.}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[obey]]
#: {{uxi|ca|Ja '''creuen''' els nens el mestre?|Do children obey the teacher?}}
# to [[believe]] {{+preo|ca|en|means=in}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Ella '''creu en''' l'amor.|She believes in love.}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[behave]]
#: {{uxi|ca|Ja '''creuen''' els nens a classe?|Do children behave in the classroom?}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to have [[faith]]

