{{head-lite|ca|verbs|cat2=defective verbs|langname=Catalan}}

# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} to [[give]]
#: {{syn-lite|ca|donar}}

====Usage notes====
While not used productively in any present variety, some verb forms of ''dar'' survive in fixed expressions:
* {{m-lite|ca|dat i beneït|lit=given and blessed}}
* {{m-lite|ca|dat i rebatut}}
* {{m-lite|ca|Déu n'hi do|lit=may God give some}}

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj}}
Some forms attested in Old Catalan:
* 1st person singular present indicative: {{m-lite|roa-oca|do}}
* 3rd person singular present indicative: {{m-lite|roa-oca|do}}
* 2nd person plural present indicative: {{m-lite|roa-oca|dau}}
* 1st person singular present subjunctive: {{m-lite|roa-oca|do}}

