Page 8756 deure: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|dēbeō|dēbēre|t=owe}} (probably through a {{inh|ca|VL.|-}} root {{m|la||*debĕre}}). Compare {{cog|oc|deure}}, {{m|oc|dever}}, {{cog|fr|devoir}}, {{cog|es|deber}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ê}}<!-- from cawikt, confirmed by GDLC and DNV -->
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-deure.wav|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ca|ɛwɾe|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[duty]], [[obligation]]

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|root=ê}}

# (transitive) to [[owe]]
# to [[have to]] (followed by an infinitive) 
#: {{syn|ca|haver de}}
# it can be assumed, it can be inferred, to be possible (followed by an infinitive)

====Usage notes====

While ''deu INFINITIVE'' as ''have to INFINTIVE'' of obligation is the general historical usage, nowadays in most of Central Catalan ''deu INFINITIVE'' has only the meaning of ''INFINTIVE can be supposed''. Compare:
: {{uxi|ca|Se'n va anar corrents, devia tenir pressa|He ran away, perhaps he was in a hurry}}
: {{uxi|ca|Se'n va anar corrents, havia de tenir pressa|He ran away, he had to be in a hurry}}

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj}}

