Page 9615 el: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|es}} {{qualifier|salat}} in Balearic dialects.
* {{alt|ca|lo}} {{qualifier|colloquial}} in North occidental dialects.

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m-lite|ca|lo}}, from {{inh-lite|ca|la|illum}}, from {{inh-lite|ca|la|ille}}. The initial ''e-'' was inserted as an {{glossary|epenthetic}} vowel after the unstressed ''-o'' had begun to be dropped.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Balearic|Central Catalan}} {{IPA-lite|ca|/əl/}}
* {{a|Valencian}} {{IPA-lite|ca|/el/}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-el.wav|Audio}}

===Article===
{{head|ca|article|g=m|feminine|la|masculine plural|els|feminine plural|les}}

# [[the]]; {{n-g-lite|definite article}}
# {{n-g-lite|neuter definite article used to make abstract nouns from adjectives}}; [[the]]; [[what]], that which
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ca|'''el''' bo i '''el''' dolent|'''the''' good and '''the''' bad}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ca|'''el''' que hem de fer|'''what''' we have to do}}

====Usage notes====
Before a word that begins with a vowel or silent ''h-'' followed by a vowel, the form {{m|ca|l'}} is used.

====See also====
* {{l-lite|ca|en}}, masculine singular definite article for given names.

===Pronoun===
{{ca-ppron|type=procl|procl_con=l'|encl=lo|encl_con='l}}

# [[him]] (direct object)

====Usage notes====
* {{U:ca:pronouns|form=reinforced}}
*: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ca|Ella '''el''' considerava estúpid.|She regarded him as stupid.}}

====Declension====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

