Page 10006 encantar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ca|la|incantō|incantāre}}, possibly taken as a semi-learned term. Equivalent to {{prefix|ca|en|cantar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# to [[enchant]], [[charm]], [[delight]]
# to [[love]], [[enjoy]]
# to [[bewitch]], put a [[spell]] on

====Usage notes====
In the sense translated as 'love', subject and object are reversed from those of ''to love''. That is, '''the subject''' of ''encantar'' is the thing that is loved and the '''indirect object''' is the person loving it. As the object is indirect, a third-person subject is supplemented with the preposition {{m|ca|a}}, or substituted by pronouns [[li#Catalan|li]]/[[els#Catalan|els]].
* M'encanta l'hivern. &mdash; I love winter a lot. (literally ''to me winter loves a lot'')

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|encantador}}
* {{l|ca|encanteri}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|cantar}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:GDLC}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}

-------- end text --------
