Numerous derivations have been proposed, including:
# from a {{inh|ca|VL.|*exiacico|*exiacicāre}}, from {{m|VL.|*iacium||bed, bedding}} (source of {{m|ca|jaç}}), from {{der|ca|la|iaceō||to lie}};
# from an [[Andalusi Arabic]] form of {{der|ca|ar|تَشَكَّى}}, frequentive/intensive of {{m|ar|شَكَا||to complain}} (source of {{m|ca|xacra}});
# from {{der|ca|la|īnstīgō|īnstīgāre|to incite, to urge}} (source of {{m|ca|instigar}});
# from a {{inh|ca|VL.|*indeago|*indeāgāre}}, alteration of {{m|la|indāgō||to track, to hunt}} (source of {{m|ca|indagar}}).

