Page 10609 -ès: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|-és||Valencia}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|-ēnsis}} (compare {{cog|oc|-és}}, {{cog|pt|-ês}}, {{cog|fr|-ais}}, {{cog|es|-és}}, {{cog|it|-ese}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Suffix===
{{ca-adj}}

# [[-ese]]; {{non-gloss definition|forms an adjective with the meaning of “pertinent thereto”}}

===Suffix===
{{ca-noun|m|f=+}}

# [[-ese]]; {{non-gloss definition|forms a noun with the meaning of “an inhabitant thereof”}}

===Suffix===
{{ca-noun|m|-}}

# [[-ese]]; {{non-gloss definition|forms a proper noun with the meaning of “the language used by the inhabitants thereof”}}

====Usage notes====
* Unlike English, where the capitalization of the proper noun is retained when a suffix is added, in Catalan, when this suffix is used with a place name, the capitalization is dropped, even when forming a language name that is itself a proper noun. Hence {{m|ca|Irlanda||Ireland}} + {{m-self|ca|-ès}} yields {{m|ca|irlandès}} not {{m|ca||*Irlandès}}.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ca}}
