====Usage notes====
By itself, {{m|ca||escocès}} usually indicates Scots, but context may indicate a different sense or even a combination of senses. In older texts, {{m|ca||escocès}} would be more likely to refer to Scottish Gaelic than to Scots. The use of {{m|ca||escocès}} for Scottish English usually only occurs among those who consider Scots to be an English dialect rather than a language of its own.

