===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|far}}~{{m|roa-oca|fair}}, from {{inh|ca|la|facio|facere}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*fakiō}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-||to put, place, set}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|[é(r)]}}<!-- per GDLC -->

====Verb====
{{ca-verb}}

# to [[make]], [[produce]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fer''' vinagre.|To make vinegar.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Aquesta terra '''fa''' molt bon blat.|This land produces very good wheat.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Quatre i quatre '''fan''' vuit.|Four and four make eight.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fer''' d'un enemic un aliat.|To turn an enemy into an ally.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fer''' [[olor]] de roses.|To smell of rose.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fer''' pudor de porcs.|To stink of pig.}}
# to [[make up]]
#: {{uxi|ca|Els jubilats '''fan''' un quart de la població.|Retired people make up a quarter of the population.}}
# to [[do]], to cause to be done
# to [[make do]]
# to [[give]]
#: {{uxi|ca|El primer marit li '''va fer''' dos fills.|Her first husband gave her two sons.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Feu'''-me mig quilo de formatge.|Give me half a kilo of cheese.}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fes'''-me un [[petó]]!|Kiss me!}}
# to [[lay]]
#: {{uxi|ca|La canària '''ha fet''' un ou.|The canary has laid an egg.}}
# to [[cause]]
# {{lb|ca|auxiliary}} to make (someone) (do something), that is {{non-gloss definition|[[auxiliary verb]] to form the [[causative]] together with an [[infinitive]]}}
#: {{uxi|ca|em '''van fer''' tornar a buscar el rebut|they '''made''' me go back to get the receipt}}
#: {{uxi|ca|l''''has feta''' plorar|you '''made''' her cry}}
# to [[go]]
# {{lb|ca|impersonal|of weather}} to [[be]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fa''' fred!|It '''is''' cold!}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fa''' calor!|It '''is''' hot!}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''Fa''' vent!|It '''is''' windy!}}
# to [[play]]
# to [[measure]]

