Page 17353 macedoni: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ca|la|Macedōnius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ò}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Millars-macedoni.wav|Audio (Valencian)}}

===Adjective===
{{ca-adj}}

# [[Macedonian]] {{gloss|pertaining to Macedonia, the Macedonian people, or the Macedonian language}}
#: {{syn|ca|macedònic}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|f=+}}

# [[Macedonian]] {{gloss|an individual from Macedonian}}
#: {{syn|ca|macedònic}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|-}}

# [[Macedonian]] {{gloss|a South Slavic language primarily spoken in Macedonia}}
#: {{syn|ca|macedònic}}

===Usage notes===
In older usage {{m|ca|macedoni}} was the term for a Macedonian person and {{m|ca|macedònic}} was the term for the adjective and the Macedonian language. In modern usage the two terms are generally considered synonymous in all senses, although some retain the traditional distinction. The modern tendency is in part caused by the fact that most such words in Catalan do triple duty as adjective, common noun, and proper noun, and is in part due to the relatively recent recognition of Macedonian as a language distinct from Bulgarian in the 19th century.

{{C|ca|Demonyms|Languages|Nationalities}}

