Page 17501 malalt: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|malalte|malate, malaute}}, from {{inh|ca|la|male habitus|t=ill-kept, run down}}.

The sound changes approximately ran as follows: *[maˈlaβtu] > [maˈlau̯te] > [maˈlaɫt]. The last stage involves a reidentification of coda [u̯] as the phoneme /l/, heavily velarized in coda positions. Cf. {{noncog|ca|colze}} < {{m|ca|colde}} < {{m|ca|*coude}} < *[ˈkoβ(e)do] < Latin {{m|la|cubitum}}.

