Page 18279 -ment: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|-ment}}, from {{inh|ca|la|mente}}, ablative singular of {{m|la|mēns||mind}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|ca|suffix}}

# {{senseid|ca|adverb}} {{n-g|added to the feminine singular form of an adjective to form an [[adverb]]; compare {{m+|en|-wise}}, {{m|en|-ly}}}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|actual|t1=current|actualment|t2=currently}}

=====Usage notes=====
In adverbs formed with the suffix {{m-self|ca|-ment}}, two syllables are stressed: the syllable that was stressed in the original adjective, and the suffix. For example, {{m|ca|ràpida|t=quick|pos=feminine singular}} yields {{m|ca|ràpidament|t=quickly}}, which is stressed {{IPAchar|/ˌra.pi.ðə.ˈmen/|lang=ca}}, as if spelled {{m|ca||ràpidamént}}.

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ca|pos=adverb}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|-ment}}, from {{inh|ca|la|-mentum}}, from earlier {{der|ca|la|-menta}}.

====Suffix====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{senseid|ca|noun}} {{n-g|forms [[nouns]] from [[verbs]]; cognate with {{l|en|-ment}}}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|patir|t1=to suffer|patiment|t2=suffering}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ca|pos=noun}}

-------- end text --------
