Page 18915 mon: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|mon}}, from {{inh|ca|VL.||*mum}}, reduced form of {{inh|ca|la|meus|meum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*meos}}. Compare {{cog|oc,fr|mon}}.

In unstressed position in Vulgar Latin {{m|la||meum, meam}} etc. were monosyllabic and regularly became {{m|ca||mon, ma}} etc. in Catalan. When stressed they were disyllabic and became {{m|ca|meu}}, {{m|roa-oca|mia}} > {{m|ca|meua}} etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Balearic|Central}} {{IPA|ca|/mun/}} {{q|always unstressed}}
* {{a|Valencian}} {{IPA|ca|/mon/}} {{q|always unstressed}}

===Determiner===
{{head|ca|determiner|cat2=possessive determiners|g=m|feminine|ma|masculine plural|mos|feminine plural|mes}}

# [[my]]

====Usage notes====
{{ca-poss-determiner-note}}

The standard masculine plural form is ''mos'', but {{m|ca|mons}} can be found in some dialects.

====Descendants====
* {{desc|scn|mo}} (''South Easy of Sicily, nearby Ragusa'')

====See also====
* {{l|ca|meu}}

