Page 19876 nos: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Inherited from the unstressed accusative of {{inh|ca|la|nōs||we; us}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*nōs}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Balearic|Central}} {{IPA|ca|/nus/}} {{q|always unstressed}}
* {{a|Valencian}} {{IPA|ca|/nos/}} {{q|always unstressed}}

====Pronoun====
{{ca-ppron|type=encl|encl_con='ns|procl=ens}}

# [[us]] (direct or indirect object)

=====Usage notes=====
* {{U:ca:pronouns|form=full}}
*: {{uxi|ca|Fes'''-nos''' una visita, si us plau!|Pay '''us''' a visit, please!}}

=====Declension=====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

===Etymology 2===
Inherited from the stressed nominative of {{inh|ca|la|nōs||we; us}}; see Etymology 1. Replaced in normal usage by {{m|ca|nosaltres}}. For the development of a distinction between stressed and unstressed forms of what was originally a single word, compare {{m+|pt|nós}} and {{m|pt|nos}}. See also the parallel development in Spanish of {{m|es|nosotros}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ca|nós||pre-2016}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ó}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|ca|pronoun}}

# {{lb|ca|archaic}} [[we]]
#: {{syn|ca|nosaltres}}
# {{lb|ca|royal|majestic}} [[we]] {{gl|the so-called [[royal we]], used by a king or queen to refer to themselves in the first person}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ó}}

====Noun====
{{head|ca|noun form}}

# {{plural of|ca|no|t=no}}

