First attested 1249.<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref> From {{der|ca|la|papȳrus}} (via a semi-learned route and adapted to a Catalan suffix<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref><ref>{{R:es:DCECH}}</ref>; cf. {{cog|ML.|paperium}}), from {{der|ca|grc|πάπυρος}}. Paper-making was introduced to Europe by the Arabs in the Middle Ages through Italy and Spain<ref>{{R:fr:TLFi|papier|etym=1}}</ref>. Compare also Old Occitan and {{cog|fr|papier}}, {{cog|oc|papièr}}, {{cog|fro|paper}}.

