Page 20975 parar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|parar}}, from {{inh|ca|la|paro|parāre}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*per-|t=produce, procure, bring forward, bring forth}}. {{etydate|13th century}}<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[stop]] (a person, an animal, a machine) from continuing movement or action
#: {{syn|ca|aturar}}
#: {{uxi|ca|no podia '''parar''' el cavall|I couldn't '''stop''' the horse}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' el cop|to avoid or mitigate the adverse consequences of something|lit=to stop the blow}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' els peus|to oppose the attitude or the actions (of somebody)|lit=to stop their feet}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''para''' el carro!|used to stop someone who rushes to say or to do something|lit=stop the cart!}} 
# {{lb|ca|intransitive|reflexive}} to [[stop]] oneself (a person, an animal, a machine) from continuing movement or action
#: {{uxi|ca|el rellotge '''s'ha parat'''|the clock '''has stopped'''}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[stop]] somewhere or at sometime (a vehicle, a person)
#: {{uxi|ca|aquest tren no '''para''' a Gavà|this train is not '''stopping''' at Gavà}}
#: {{uxi|ca|'''parem''' al migdia per dinar|we '''stop''' at noon to have lunch}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|sense '''parar'''|without any interruption|lit=without stopping}}
# to [[stop]] doing {{+preo|ca|de|infinitive}}
#: {{syn|ca|acabar}}
#: {{uxi|ca|quan '''pari''' de xerrar|when he/she '''stops''' chatting}}
# {{lb|ca|impersonal}} to [[stop]] [[happen]]ing {{+preo|ca|de|infinitive}}
#: {{uxi|ca|ja '''ha parat''' de ploure|rain is over}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[hold out]], to [[extend]] (a hand, a bag etc) to [[receive]] something
#: {{uxi|ca|'''para''' el davantal per recollir les cireres!|'''extend''' the apron to collect the cherries!}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' l'esquena|to '''resign''' oneself to receive a reprimand etc|lit=to offer the back}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' la galta|to '''expose''' oneself to receive either a compliment or a punishment|lit=to offer the cheek}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' la mà|to '''accept''' money as a reward|lit=to extend the hand}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[prepare]] or [[set up]] something to make it available to function or to serve a purpose. 
#: {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' una trampa|to '''prepare''' a [[trap]] so that it is ready to operate and catch something or somebody}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' taula|to '''set''' the {{l|en|table}}, to arrange the utensils necessary for eating|lit=to '''set up''' the table}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' l'orella|to listen carefully|lit=to '''set up''' one's ear}}
#: {{lb|ca|idiomatic}} {{uxi|ca|'''parar''' compte|to pay attention (to something)|lit=to '''set up''' account}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[endure]] something adverse
#: {{uxi|ca|vam haver de '''parar''' el sol|we had to '''endure''' the sun}}
# to have the "it" role in chasing games like {{l|en|tag}} or the like
#: {{uxi|ca|tu '''pares'''!|'''tag''', you're "It"!.}}
# to [[end up]] in a place, in a state
#: {{syn|ca|acabar}}, {{syn|ca|estar}}, {{syn|ca|quedar}}, {{syn|ca|restar}}
#: {{uxi|ca|on '''para''' el nen?|where did the boy '''end up'''?}}
#: {{uxi|ca|la pilota ha anat a '''parar''' a la teulada|the ball has landed on the roof}}
#: {{uxi|ca|per on '''pares'''?|where are you? (now)}}
# to [[stay]], [[reside]] temporarily, while in a town
#: {{syn|ca|estar}}-se
#: {{uxi|ca|on '''pares''' a Olot?|where are you '''staying''' when in Olot?}}

