Page 22033 plaer: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|pler}}
* {{alt|ca|plaier||dialectal|Algherese}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|plaer}}~{{m|roa-oca|plader}}~{{m|roa-oca|plaser}}~{{m|roa-oca|plazer}}, from {{inh|ca|la|placeo|placēre}}.

The Old Catalan word was mainly used as a verb, "to please", and this was later replaced by the likely analogical form {{m|ca|plaure}},<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref> while the original infinitive was maintained in a more abstract and noun form: compare a similar development in {{cog|fr|plaisir||pleasure}} vs. {{m|fr|plaire||to please}}. Compare also the noun use of {{cog|oc|plaser||pleasure}}, {{cog|it|piacere}}, {{cog|es|placer}}, {{cog|ro|plăcere}}, etc., from the Latin infinitive.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|[ê(r)]}}<!-- from cawikt; /ɛ/ confirmed for Central by GDLC -->

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[pleasure]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|plaure}}

===References===
<references/>

