# A sheep, goat, or bovine from the time it has lost its [[milk teeth]] until these are replaced with a second adult set (i.e. older than a year but less than three years of age).

====Usage notes====
For sheep, the first set of adult teeth appear at about 14 months and are lost between 20 and 24 months of age. Before this time they are called {{m|ca|borrecs}}/{{m|ca|borregues}} and afterwards they are called {{m|ca|terçats}}/{{m|ca|terçades}}.

