===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|ca|la|pungō|t=to puncture}}, either analogically derived from Catalan {{m|ca|punxí}}, from the perfect form of the Latin verb<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref>, or through a {{der|ca|VL.|*punctiāre}}, itself possibly reaching Catalan (and the Spanish equivalent {{m|es|punchar}}) through a Valencian Mozarabic intermediate<ref>{{R:es:DCECH}}</ref>. Compare also {{cog|es|punzar}}, {{m|es|pinchar}}, and {{cog|oc|ponchar}}.

