Page 23442 quilo-: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|ca|fr|kilo-}}, from {{der|ca|grc|χίλιοι||thousand}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ca|kilo-}}

====Prefix====
{{head|ca|prefix}}

# [[kilo-]] {{gloss|SI prefix expressing 10<sup>3</sup> of the base unit}}

=====Usage notes=====
The letter {{m|mul|k}} is not normally used in Catalan. Instead, Catalan orthography calls for using the {{m|mul|qu}} digraph to represent the {{IPAchar|/k/}} sound before an {{m|mul|e}} or an {{m|mul|i}}. Therefor, when the metric system was introduced into Catalan, the prefix {{m|fr|kilo-}} was originally spelled {{m|ca||quilo-}}. With the advent of {{m|mul|k}} as a standard international abbreviation, usage of {{m|ca|kilo-}} has become not only acceptable, but also more common than the traditional spelling. However, traditionalists still insist upon the use of {{m|ca||quilo-}}.

=====Derived terms=====
{{prefixsee|ca}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|ca|grc|χεῖλος||lip, edge}}.

====Prefix====
{{head|ca|prefix|before a vowel|quil-}}

# [[cheilo-]] {{gloss|combining form used in scientific neologisms to indicate the lips or an edge}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|quiloplàstia|gloss=cheiloplasty}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|ca|grc|χυλός||secretion, bile}}.

====Prefix====
{{head|ca|prefix|before a vowel|quil-}}

# [[chole-]] {{gloss|combining form used in scientific neologisms to indicate bile}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|quilopericardi|gloss=presence of bile in the pericardial fluid}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|col-|gloss=relating to bile}}
* {{l|ca|quil|gloss=bile}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}

