Page 24409 resar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ca|es|rezar}}, from {{der|ca|la|recito|recītāre|t=recite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|root=é}}

# to [[pray]]
# to [[officiate]] in a religious service

====Usage notes====
In its original sense, {{m|ca|resar}} meant to read an oration: hence a {{m|ca|missa resada}} is a mass which is read rather than sung ("low mass"). It has come to be used in the sense of to pray, especially when referring to non-Christian religions, in preference to the verb {{m|ca|pregar}}, which has taken on a more mundane sense.

