====Usage notes====
* The term {{m|ca||romaní|Romany, Roma}} is of recent coinage in Catalan, reflecting the {{glossary|endonym}} of the Roma. The older {{glossary|exonym}}, {{m|ca|gitano||Gypsy}}, is still popular.
* The {{m|ca|IEC}} and {{m|ca|AVL}} disagree over the proper plural of {{m|ca||romaní}}. The AVL has chosen to prescribe the regular plural {{m|ca||romanins}} as if the term had a Latin derivation, while the IEC has chosen to prescribe the plural form {{m|ca||romanís}}.

