Page 25658 seny: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ca|2018|August|7}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ê}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|sen}}, from {{inh|ca|VL.|*sennus}}, from {{der|ca|frk|*sinn}}, possibly influenced by {{noncog|la|sensus||sense}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[sense]], [[common sense]], [[sensibleness]]
#: {{syn|ca|sentit|judici|senderi|trellat}}
#: {{ant|ca|rauxa}}
#* {{quote-book|ca|year=2011|author=Jaume Vallcorba i Rocosa|title=Obra gramatical i lingüística completa|publisher=L'Abadia de Montserrat|isbn=9788498833591|page=33
|passage=Quan no obrem d'acord amb el '''seny''' ho sabem: és quan hem fet les coses, per un desig, per un impuls o, en fi, per una passió, petita o grossa, temptadora o abassegadora.
|t=When we don't act in accordance with '''common sense''', we know it: it's when we've done things for a desire, for an urge, or, in short, for a passion; small or great, tempting or engrossing.}}
# {{lb|ca|obsolete}} [[sense]], [[sensory]] [[perception]]
#: {{syn|ca|sentit}}
#* {{quote-text|ca|year=1968|author=Rodolfo Llorena y Jordana|title=Com han estat i com som els catalans
|passage=Esclaus dels cinc '''senys''' corporals: veure, oir, olorar, gustar i palpar, que configuren el món i la vida.
|translation=[We are] slaves to the five bodily '''senses''': seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting and touching, which shape the world and life.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|assenyat}}
* {{l|ca|forassenyat}}
* {{l|ca|queixal del seny}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|seny}}, from {{inh|ca|la|signum||signal}}, of {{der|ca|ine-pro|-}} origin. The meaning of "bell" is attested from the 6th century onwards. Doublet of the borrowing {{doublet|ca|signe|notext=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|archaic}} [[sign]]
#: {{syn|ca|senyal}}
# {{lb|ca|archaic}} large [[bell]]
#: {{syn|ca|campana}}
#* {{quote-text|ca|year=1908|author=Joan Segura|title=Historia d'Igualada|page=150
|passage=Lo '''seny''' del lladre era un toch de campana que's feya al cap-vespre. Per broma devía dirse'n lo '''seny''' del lladre, com si diguessen que al fer aquell toch començava la nit, la hora deis lladres.
|translation=The thief '''bell''' was the a bell that tolled at nightfall. As a joke it was to be called the thief '''bell''', as if to say that when it tolls, night, the time of thieves, began.}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|senya}}
* {{l|ca|senyera}}

