Page 25829 seu: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|sou}} (feminine {{m|roa-oca|sua}}), from {{inh|ca|la|suus|suum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*sowos}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*sewos}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*swé||self}}. The original stem was modified by analogy with {{m|ca|meu}}.

The weak form {{m|ca|son}} is also from {{inh|ca|la|suus|suum}} in an unstressed (monosyllabic) position.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ca|sou||Algherese}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|é}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|ca|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns|feminine|seva|or|seua|masculine plural|seus|feminine plural|seves|or|seues}}

# [[his]], [[her]]/[[hers]], [[its]]
# [[their]], [[theirs]]
# [[your]], [[yours]] (alluding to {{m|ca|vostè}} or {{m|ca|vostès}})

=====Usage notes=====
* When preceding a noun, {{m|ca||seu}} is always preceded by the appropriate definite article.
* The third person possessive changes form for number and gender according to the number and gender of the ''item possessed'', not the number and gender of the possessor.

=====Declension=====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|ca|son}}
* {{l|ca|llur}}

