===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|sortir}} (compare {{cog|oc|sortir}}), from {{inh|ca|la|sortior|sortīrī|t=select}}, probably influenced by {{m|la|surrectus}} (through a {{inh|ca|VL.|-}} form {{m|la||*surctus}} and its derivatives, possibly through a verb {{m|la||*surrectīre, surctīre}}; cf. also Old Catalan {{m|ca|surt}}, {{m|ca|surta}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{homophones|ca|sortí}}
* {{rhymes|ca|i(ɾ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# to [[go out]], to [[leave]]
#: {{syn|ca|marxar|eixir|q2=chiefly Valencian}}
#: {{ant|ca|entrar}}
# to [[go out]] {{gloss|to leave one's abode to go to public places, especially for recreation or entertainment}}
# to [[come out]], to [[appear]], to [[emerge]]
#: {{syn|ca|aparèixer|emergir}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Ja li han sortit '''arrugues''' a la cara.|Wrinkles have already appeared on his/her face.}}
# to [[come out]], to be [[published]], to be [[make known|made known]]
# to [[end up]], to [[turn out]]
#: {{uxi|ca|'''sortir''' bé|to '''come out''' well}}
# {{lb|ca|reflexive|pronominal}} to manage to get out of a difficult situation successfully {{ngd|(requires a reflexive pronoun according the subject, and the appropriate form of the adverbial pronoun [[en#Catalan|en]])}}
#: {{uxi|ca|Ho tenia difícil, però '''se'n va sortir''' prou bé|It was difficult for him, but he did well enough}}


