#: {{syn|ca|salari}}
#: {{uxi|ca|tinc un '''sou''' de 1200 euros|I have a '''salary''' of 1200 euros}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ó}}
* {{rhymes|ca|ow|s=1}}

====Verb====
{{head|ca|verb form}}

# {{ca-verb form of|ser}}
# {{ca-verb form of|ésser}}

===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|sou}} (feminine {{m|roa-oca|sua}}), from {{inh|ca|la|suus|suum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*sowos}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*sewos}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*swé||self}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ca|seu||non-Algherese dialects}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|ó}}
* {{rhymes|ca|ow|s=1}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|ca|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns|feminine|sua|masculine plural|sous|feminine plural|sues}}
# {{lb|ca|Algherese}} [[your]], [[yours]] (singular, alluding to {{m|ca|vostè}})
# {{lb|ca|Algherese}} [[his]], [[her]]/[[hers]], [[its]]
# {{lb|ca|Algherese|archaic|rare}} [[their]], [[theirs]]

=====Usage notes=====
In contemporary Algherese, this word primarily gives reference to ''vostè''. Only rarely does it give reference to multiple possessors, this use being archaic.

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|ca|seu}}
* {{desc|scn|sou|sua|soi|so'}}

