Page 26448 suar: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|sudar||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|suar}}, from {{inh|ca|la|sudo|sūdāre}}, a verb based ultimately on {{der|ca|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}. Compare {{cog|oc|susar}}, {{m|oc|suar}}, {{m|oc|sudar}}; {{cog|fr|suer}}; {{cog|es|sudar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[sweat]]
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} (figurative) to [[exude]] humidity
#: {{uxi|ca|la paret '''sua'''|the wall is exuding humidity}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} (figurative) to [[strive]], to [[try hard]]
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to exude some other liquid
#: {{uxi|ca|'''suar''' sang|to exude blood}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to get wet of sweat
#: {{uxi|ca|'''suar''' la camisa|to get wet one's shirt}}
#:: (idiomatic) {{uxi|ca|'''suar''' la cansalada|to try really hard to achieve something}} (literally ''to sweat the bacon'')
# {{lb|ca|reflexive}} to get wet of sweat
#: {{uxi|ca|estic tot '''suat'''|I'm all sweaty}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} (figurative) to earn something by hard working
#: {{uxi|ca|si ho vols, ho hauràs de '''suar'''|If you want it, you'll need to work hard to get it}}

