Page 27573 tocar el dos: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{lit|to touch the back}}, from archaic {{m+|ca|dos||back}}, to tap the back of a horse or other transport animals to encourage them to move forward.

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|root=ò}}

# {{lb|ca|idiom}} to [[leave]]; to [[up and leave]]; to [[scram]]

====Usage notes====
Because ''dos'' is an obsolete spelling of {{m|ca|dors||back}}, the literal meaning is sometimes interpreted as "touch the two" by those not aware of the history.
