Page 28023 trencar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|trencar}}, itself possibly from a {{inh|ca|VL.|*trinicāre|t=cut into three parts}}, from the root {{m|la|trini}}, based on {{m|la|duplicāre}}, or alternatively from an alteration of {{inh|ca|la|truncāre}}. It may also derive from or be influenced by a pre-Roman, possibly {{der|ca|cel-gau|-}} word, cf. {{m|cel-gau||*trincare|t=cut the head}}, or a base {{m|cel-gau||*trenko}}. Compare {{cog|oc|trencar}}, {{cog|fr|trancher}}, {{cog|fro|trenchier}}, {{cog|gl|trincar}}, {{cog|pt|trincar}} and {{cog|it|troncare}}. Native doublet of {{doublet|ca|trinxar|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=2}}

