===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|veure}}, from {{inh|ca|la|videō|vidēre}} (with a change in verb class), from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*widēō}}, from {{der|ca|ine-pro|*weyd-||to know; see}}. Old Catalan {{m|roa-oca|veher}} and {{m|roa-oca|veser}} continued the Latin {{m|la||vidēre}} directly.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ê}}<!-- from cawikt, confirmed by GDLC and DNV -->
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-veure.wav|Audio}}
* {{homophones|ca|beure}}
* {{rhymes|ca|ɛwɾe|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|root=ê}}

# to [[see]]
# to [[find]] (someone or something to be a certain way)
#: {{ux|ca|Et '''veig''' una mica estressat.|You seem [lit. I '''find''' you] a little stressed.}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive|hi}} (with pronoun ''hi'') to be able to [[see]]
#: {{uxi|ca|Que '''hi veu''' bé?|Can you see ok?}}
# {{lb|ca|pronominal}} to [[look]], to [[appear]]
#: {{ux|ca|Penses que '''em veig''' bonica? &mdash; Sí, '''et veus''' increïble!|Do think '''I look''' nice? &mdash; Yes, '''you look''' incredible!}}

