Page 29332 vostè: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|vosté||Valencian}}

===Etymology===
Contraction of {{m|ca|vostre|vostra|your}} {{m|ca|mercè||grace}}. {{etydate|16th century}}<ref>{{R:ca:GDLC}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Pronoun===
{{ca-ppron|type=strong}}

# [[you]] {{q|formal, singular}}
#: {{syn|ca|tu|q1=common|vós|q2=formal}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ca||Vostè}} is a very polite form of address for a single person. It is used with the ''third''-person singular form of the verb. (Compare the polite usage of {{m|pt|você}} in Portuguese and {{m|es|usted}} in Spanish.) Traditionally it was only used with judges, doctors, and so on, with {{m|ca|vós}} being used in most polite situations, for example with elderly people, and {{m|ca|tu}} being used in informal situations. Nowadays, {{m|ca||tu}} is the most common form, even in formal contexts, and {{m|ca||vostè}} is becoming more common than {{m|ca||vós}} because of contact with Spanish. In Valencian, this word is usually spelled ''vosté'', since it has /e/ instead of /ɛ/.

====Declension====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:ca:IEC2}}
* {{R:ca:DNV}}
* {{R:ca:DCVB}}
-------- end text --------
Page 29333 vosté: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|vostè||standard}}

===Etymology===
Contraction of {{m|ca|vostre|vostra|your}} {{m|ca|mercè||forgiveness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Valencian}} {{IPA|ca|/vosˈte/}}
* {{rhymes|ca|e|s=2}}

===Pronoun===
{{ca-ppron|type=strong}}

# [[you]] (formal, singular)
#: {{syn|ca|tu<q:common>|;|vós<q:formal>}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ca||Vosté}} is a very polite form of address for a single person. It is used with the ''third''-person singular form of the verb. (Compare the polite usage of {{m|es|usted}} in Spanish.) Traditionally it was only used with judges, doctors, and so on, with {{m|ca|vós}} being used in most polite situations, for example with elderly people, and {{m|ca|tu}} being used in informal situations. Nowadays, {{m|ca||tu}} is the most common form, even in formal contexts, and {{m|ca||vosté}} is becoming more common than {{m|ca||vós}} because of contact with Spanish. In Catalonia, this word is usually spelled vostè, since it has /ɛ/ instead of /e/.

====Declension====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

-------- end text --------
